WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.920
A link opens on a phone.

00:00:02.615 --> 00:00:03.395
A video plays.

00:00:03.755 --> 00:00:04.735
A web page runs.

00:00:05.135 --> 00:00:06.695
A write-up reads like a page.

00:00:07.403 --> 00:00:09.883
Nothing to download, and no app to install.

00:00:11.605 --> 00:00:12.805
This is Markdrop.

00:00:12.825 --> 00:00:13.865
Your desk, as links.

00:00:15.537 --> 00:00:17.497
Write or paste Markdown, and publish.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:18.737
You don't need an account.

00:00:19.472 --> 00:00:23.612
Tables, code, diagrams and math all render, and you can name the link.

00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:27.395
Files get the same treatment.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:34.709
HTML pages, PDFs, spreadsheets, Word documents, and videos up to two gigabytes.

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:37.069
Each one opens in a viewer made for it.

00:00:38.964 --> 00:00:44.844
An uploaded page runs, scripts and all, from a separate domain, so it can't reach your Markdrop account.

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.661
Found a mistake after you shared it?

00:00:49.061 --> 00:00:51.101
Edit the document, or replace the file.

00:00:51.668 --> 00:00:56.568
The link stays the same, open pages update, and the last five versions are kept.

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:04.064
Then choose who can open it: anyone with the link, your team, or only people you add by email.

00:01:04.749 --> 00:01:07.309
Add a password or an expiry if you need one.

00:01:09.331 --> 00:01:13.071
For a document only its readers should see, encrypt it in your browser.

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:16.999
The key stays in the link, and our servers never receive it.

00:01:19.377 --> 00:01:25.057
Once you're signed in, you see how it's read: views, how far people got, and where a video lost them.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:28.052
Totals and patterns, never who someone is.

00:01:30.112 --> 00:01:35.732
Teams get a workspace: shared folders, roles, and your own domain, with your logo on the pages.

00:01:38.079 --> 00:01:40.139
And you can publish from where you already work.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:44.133
The VS Code extension keeps a file in sync both ways.

00:01:44.639 --> 00:01:46.539
The command line uploads big files.

00:01:47.151 --> 00:01:50.271
And AI apps like Claude can publish and update links for you.

00:01:52.166 --> 00:01:57.366
When a file shouldn't live anywhere, send it straight to another device, or to up to ten people.

00:01:57.892 --> 00:01:59.372
It's never stored on our servers.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.480
And for docs, there's Markdrop Guides.

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:09.967
It shows where readers drop off, ranks what to fix, and drafts the fix for you to review.

00:02:12.244 --> 00:02:14.724
Bring your docs in from GitHub, and stay in sync.

00:02:15.247 --> 00:02:18.487
Put live demos, video and PDFs in the page.

00:02:19.047 --> 00:02:20.147
Keep some pages private.

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:24.247
Readers get Ask AI, and agents get an MCP server.

00:02:26.451 --> 00:02:27.571
Markdrop.

00:02:27.591 --> 00:02:29.851
Drop something in, at markdrop.in.
